{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"Swidux","title":"Swidux","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"Swidux-logo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop."}]},{"text":"Companion Packages","type":"heading","anchor":"Companion-Packages","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a prev